05"&gt;Fossday - Lajeado - 2018/05/05&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;First workshop presented about how to use Docker in a &amp;ldquo;minimum way&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Dockerfile&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Volumes&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Docker Compose&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="slides"&gt;Slides&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe src="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/e/2PACX-1vQFwP-bT78vkYG8_tFGm3QHt2BG44QXwcVhc-_bRQuh-vWCCE0k9GR6K_5xqXwvB3FXn0-lMsvyqyWU/embed?start=false&amp;loop=false&amp;delayms=3000" frameborder="0" width="480" height="299" allowfullscreen="true" mozallowfullscreen="true" webkitallowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</description></item><item><title>Configuration management</title><link>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-10-03-poatek-configuration-management/</link><pubDate>Tue, 03 Oct 2017 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-10-03-poatek-configuration-management/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="configuration-management"&gt;Configuration Management&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="poatek---porto-alegre---20171003"&gt;Poatek - Porto Alegre - 2017/10/03&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Brief introduction of how we can use Puppet to managem things.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Changing granulatiry&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Imutable environment&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;What is the real motive to use configuration management&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="slides"&gt;Slides&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe src="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/e/2PACX-1vSPU4Foq_7_cVu4bpR_x7lRWLFfjN-BZ-Ou0ZHSJfT9Urw6FwkPRygu9zAAPdgFauhdnUshxbu7wJHi/embed?start=false&amp;loop=true&amp;delayms=3000" frameborder="0" width="480" height="299" allowfullscreen="true" mozallowfullscreen="true" webkitallowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</description></item><item><title>Introduction to Puppet</title><link>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-09-02-agco-introduction-to-puppet/</link><pubDate>Sat, 02 Sep 2017 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-09-02-agco-introduction-to-puppet/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction-to-puppet"&gt;Introduction to Puppet&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="agco-canoas---canoas---20170902"&gt;AGCO Canoas - Canoas - 2017/09/02&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The ideia is to show how we can delivery better environments using patterns and same environment reproduction, having change management with confiability.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="slides"&gt;Slides&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe src="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/e/2PACX-1vTrBU9r28ng9suZu6YGPFLPJzdxSSLB65uJcCMTPaJuQ4Q53cY9EfR2zcx1qJYO5qhINI_mUQXDLKtS/embed?start=false&amp;loop=true&amp;delayms=3000" frameborder="0" width="480" height="299" allowfullscreen="true" mozallowfullscreen="true" webkitallowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</description></item><item><title>Puppet Administration</title><link>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-09-02-agco-puppet-administration/</link><pubDate>Sat, 02 Sep 2017 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-09-02-agco-puppet-administration/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="puppet-administration"&gt;Puppet Administration&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="agco-canoas---canoas---20170902"&gt;AGCO Canoas - Canoas - 2017/09/02&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In this apresentation we used the basics of &amp;ldquo;resources&amp;rdquo; statement, like package, service and file.&#10;This apresentation was for the infrastructure team.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="slides"&gt;Slides&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe src="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/e/2PACX-1vRTdxBe-hmKoo6KKpTPXHKzp8-SNUg6Qu-QGvA33tYU7YQF70Olau3TOaPRzHVRQgURrwZtWedw-I8j/embed?start=false&amp;loop=true&amp;delayms=3000" frameborder="0" width="480" height="299" allowfullscreen="true" mozallowfullscreen="true" webkitallowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</description></item><item><title>Docker Introduction</title><link>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-04-29-tchelinux-docker-introduction/</link><pubDate>Sat, 29 Apr 2017 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-04-29-tchelinux-docker-introduction/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="docker-introduction"&gt;Docker introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="tchê-linux-lajeado---lajeadors---univates---20170429"&gt;Tchê Linux Lajeado - Lajeado/RS - UNIVATES - 2017/04/29&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="summary-of-the-lecture"&gt;Summary of the lecture&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Docker changes how we create systems. Reasons for your adoption are many, but here is some good examples:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Embedded application&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Same environments&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Patterns as best practices&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Community&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;With just a few commands, we can have our application online on the most biggest cloud providers, like: AWS, Google Cloud, Digital Ocean, OpenStack and many others. We have an application embedded, so the deployment is very simplified.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Docker Introduction</title><link>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-02-22-poatek-docker-introduction/</link><pubDate>Wed, 22 Feb 2017 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://rafaeldutra.me/en/presentations/2017-02-22-poatek-docker-introduction/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="docker-introduction"&gt;Docker introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="poatek---porto-alegre---20170222"&gt;Poatek - Porto Alegre - 2017/02/22&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="summary"&gt;Summary&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Community&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Breve história&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;What&amp;rsquo;s Docker&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Container is NOT VM&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Why should used it&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Demo&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="slides"&gt;Slides&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe src="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1-2StfxZVM5UChe2z4dqiPhtLZMDdzWPK18k5yJB62EA/embed?start=false&amp;loop=false&amp;delayms=3000" frameborder="0" width="480" height="299" allowfullscreen="true" mozallowfullscreen="true" webkitallowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>